---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { getContactLinks } from "../lib/site-content";

const contact = await getContactLinks();
const EFFECTIVE_DATE = "23 September 2026";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions — Sunflora"
  description="The terms that apply when you browse, order from, or otherwise use the Sunflora website."
  effectiveDate={EFFECTIVE_DATE}
>
  <Fragment slot="title">Terms &amp; Conditions</Fragment>

  <p>
    These Terms &amp; Conditions ("Terms") govern your use of
    sunfloracrochet.in (the "Site") and any order you place with Sunflora
    ("Sunflora", "we", "us", "our"), a home-based handmade crochet studio
    operated by Aru Jaiswal, based in Siwan, Bihar, India. By browsing the
    Site or placing an order, you agree to these Terms. If you don't agree,
    please don't use the Site.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who can order</h2>
  <p>
    You must be at least 18 years old, or place orders under the supervision
    of a parent or legal guardian, to order from Sunflora. By placing an
    order you confirm this is the case and that the information you give us
    is accurate.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Our products</h2>
  <p>
    Every piece is handmade to order. Because of this:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      slight variations in colour, size, stitch pattern and finish between
      the product photo and the piece you receive are normal, not a defect
      — that's the nature of something made by hand rather than a machine;
    </li>
    <li>
      colours may also appear slightly different depending on your screen;
    </li>
    <li>
      soft toys and amigurumi may include small parts (eyes, embellishments)
      and are not intended for children under 3 without adult supervision.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Pricing and payment</h2>
  <p>
    All prices on the Site are listed in Indian Rupees (₹) and are inclusive
    of applicable taxes unless stated otherwise. Payments are processed
    securely through our payment partner, Razorpay; we do not see or store
    your card, UPI or bank account details. An order is confirmed only once
    payment has been successfully received.
  </p>
  <p>
    We reserve the right to correct any pricing error and to cancel an order
    placed at an incorrect price, in which case we will refund any payment
    already made in full.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Order acceptance and cancellation</h2>
  <p>
    Placing an order is an offer to buy; we may accept, decline, or cancel
    an order — for example if an item has become unavailable, we suspect
    fraud, or delivery isn't possible to your location. If we cancel an
    order after payment, we will refund you in full.
  </p>
  <p>
    Because pieces are made to order, cancellation windows and any
    applicable cancellation charges are as described at checkout and in our
    <a href="/faq">FAQ</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Custom orders</h2>
  <p>
    Custom orders are made based on the description, references or images
    you provide. Please make sure any reference material you send us is
    something you have the right to share. Turnaround times, deposits and
    revision terms for custom pieces are as communicated to you at the time
    of the request — see our <a href="/custom">Custom Orders</a> page and
    <a href="/faq">FAQ</a> for current details.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Shipping, returns and refunds</h2>
  <p>
    Shipping timelines, charges, and our returns/refund/exchange policy are
    set out in our <a href="/faq#shipping">Shipping &amp; Delivery</a> and
    <a href="/faq#returns">Returns &amp; Refunds</a> FAQ sections, which form
    part of these Terms. As handmade, made-to-order items, custom pieces
    are generally not eligible for change-of-mind returns; damaged or
    incorrect items are covered as described there.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your account</h2>
  <p>
    We use passwordless "magic link" sign-in — you're responsible for
    keeping access to the email address linked to your account secure, and
    for all activity that happens through it. Tell us right away at
    <a href={contact.mailto}>{contact.email}</a> if you suspect unauthorised
    use of your account.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Reviews and content you submit</h2>
  <p>
    If you submit a product review, comment, or other content to us (for
    example, a photo of a custom piece), you confirm it's your own and you
    grant Sunflora a non-exclusive, royalty-free licence to display it on
    the Site and our social media, for as long as it remains posted. Please
    keep reviews honest and respectful — we may remove content that is
    abusive, fraudulent, or unrelated to the product.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    All designs, photographs, text and branding on the Site belong to
    Sunflora unless stated otherwise, and may not be copied, reproduced or
    used commercially without our written permission.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>use the Site for any unlawful purpose or to place fraudulent orders;</li>
    <li>attempt to interfere with the Site's security or normal operation; or</li>
    <li>scrape, copy or resell content or product listings from the Site without permission.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>11. Liability</h2>
  <p>
    We provide the Site and our products with reasonable care and skill.
    To the extent permitted by law, Sunflora is not liable for indirect or
    consequential loss arising from your use of the Site, and our total
    liability for any claim relating to an order is limited to the amount
    you paid for that order. Nothing in these Terms limits any right you
    have under the Consumer Protection Act, 2019 that cannot lawfully be
    excluded.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Governing law and grievance redressal</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms are governed by the laws of India. Subject to applicable
    consumer-protection law giving you the right to approach a forum closer
    to you, courts having jurisdiction over Siwan, Bihar shall have
    exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute.
  </p>
  <p>
    For any complaint regarding an order or these Terms, please contact our
    Grievance Officer:
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Aru Jaiswal</strong><br />
    Sunflora, Siwan, Bihar, India<br />
    Email: <a href={contact.mailto}>{contact.email}</a><br />
    WhatsApp: <a href={contact.whatsappUrl}>{contact.phoneDisplay}</a>
  </p>

  <h2>13. Changes to these Terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these Terms from time to time. Changes take effect once
    posted here with an updated effective date; continuing to use the Site
    after that means you accept the updated Terms.
  </p>

  <hr />
  <p>
    See also our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> and
    <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
